From d77617f514cf4ec8cfb0233bb649d20aa260d0b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "MOTOR-47 (Claude)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:28:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FlyWeb 3.2.0 interface: URL field and suggestions popup as
 one piece
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Titín (20-11, bt-320e and maqueta-oscuro-desplegable-hd.webp): with the
URL focused, the suggestions popup is as wide as the URL field, sits
right below it, has no outer shadow, and both share a very subtle corner
radius instead of a pill. In every window, private ones included
(Titín).

- RoundedOmniboxResultsFrame: no location bar alignment insets
  (Chromium: 6 dip on each side and 5 dip above and below), a cutout as
  high as the field (kLocationBarHeight minus kFlyWebLocationBarTopTrim:
  since 0009 the 3 dip difference left a transparent band under the
  field), elevation 0 and the field's radius. Two hooks in a new patch.
- LocationBarView::ComputeBorderRadius() returns
  kFlyWebLocationBarCornerRadius (2 dip, about 1-2 px on the mockups);
  one hook more in its patch. BraveLocationBarView::GetBorderRadius()
  follows it, so the inner glow and the focus ring do too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MwmK2hjxRPyuefYzGRoZRk
